  'Event Loop Execution Order',
  'node-event-loop-order',
  'Given a list of operations — "SYNC label", "PROMISE label" (microtask), or "TIMEOUT label ms" (macrotask) — output the labels in the order Node.js would actually execute them: all synchronous code first (in code order), then all resolved promises/microtasks (in code order), then timers (ordered by delay, ties by code order).',
